# Scripts in this repo are executed inside a Linux container. A CRLF checkout
# on Windows breaks them with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", so line
# endings are normalised to LF for everything textual.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
x      text eol=lf
*.rs   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

*.pdf binary

# Model and texture data. `text=auto` above relies on Git guessing which files
# are binary, and a single newline rewritten inside a .glb corrupts the whole
# model - the same class of failure as the ^M in shell scripts above, but
# silent, because a broken .glb fails at load time rather than at checkout.
*.glb  binary
*.gltf binary
*.bin  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
